    "scope": "Detailed function-level create-order flow entering CreateOrderController.handle. Covers createOrder, reserve, charge, authorize, saveOrder, release, paired returns, empty-order and invalid-total validation, success, catch cleanup, pre-catch reserve failure, and cleanup failure propagation. Both views retain identical call and error coverage. Local Map operations and reservation-id conversion are supporting facts, not separate service lifelines. Excludes unrelated controllers, external callers, runtime routing, and nonexistent network/database integrations.",
    "notes": [
      "ProviderClient and both Maps are local; no external payment or database integration is present.",
      "reserve executes before try; its rejection bypasses release.",
      "saveOrder and release have no explicit throw; their rejection branches show conditional propagation.",
      "A release rejection replaces the original error because throw error is not reached.",
      "No retries or payment refunds are implemented.",
      "Direct source tracing; runtime routing, injected behavior, and execution were not verified."
    ]
